+/*
+ * SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
+ * Copyright (c) 2026, Friedt Professional Engineering Services, Inc.
+ *
+ * stress-ng feature configuration for Zephyr.
+ *
+ * Makefile.config normally writes config.h after probing the build host with
+ * the programs under test/. On Zephyr what is available is decided by Kconfig,
+ * so this file maps Kconfig symbols onto the HAVE_* macros instead: each
+ * POSIX function is enabled by the Option Group that implements it, the
+ * toolchain features by the architecture. It was seeded by compiling the
+ * test/ probes with the Zephyr SDK against the posix-next headers for
+ * qemu_x86, qemu_x86_64, qemu_cortex_a53, qemu_riscv32, qemu_riscv64 and
+ * mps2/an385, then linking every declared function to find the ones that
+ * have no implementation (zephyr/scripts/gen_config.py).
+ */
